      <p>If you call us, we may note the same kinds of details. {% pending "whether calls are recorded. If they are, this must be stated here and at the start of the call." %}</p>

      <h2 id="not-collect">What we do not ask for</h2>
      <p>With an enquiry, we do not ask for portal passwords, OTPs, PAN or Aadhaar scans, bank statements or tax filings. If work goes ahead, the records it needs, and a secure way to share them, are agreed with you at that point.</p>

      <h2 id="share">Who may see your details</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AccountOrbit ({{ site.owner.name }}),</strong> to discuss your requirement and coordinate the next steps.</li>
        <li><strong>Another professional who may carry out part of your work,</strong> only if you have ticked the separate sharing box or agreed by phone. Once they have your details, their own privacy practices also apply, so ask them.</li>
        <li><strong>Service providers we use to run the enquiry system,</strong> which will be named here before the online form opens. {% pending "the form processor, hosting and any other processors, and where they store data." %}</li>
        <li><strong>Authorities,</strong> where the law requires it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>{% pending "whether any professional pays AccountOrbit in connection with a customer's work, which this policy would then need to disclose." %}</p>

      <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
      <p>India's Digital Personal Data Protection framework gives you the right to withdraw consent as easily as you gave it, to exercise your rights under the Act, and to complain to the Data Protection Board. We intend to meet this standard from the day the form opens, even if some of its requirements take effect later.</p>
      <p>To ask about your details, call {{ site.phoneDisplay }}. The formal route for withdrawing consent and for access, correction and deletion requests, with response times, will be set out here when this policy is finalised. {% pending "the exact route for withdrawing consent, asking to see, correct or delete your details, and making a complaint, with response times." %}</p>
      <p>If a professional already has your details, withdrawing consent with us does not by itself remove them from that professional's records. Ask them directly as well. {% pending "whether AccountOrbit will pass on such requests." %}</p>

      <h2 id="keep">How long we keep details</h2>
      <p>The retention period for enquiry details will be stated here when this policy is finalised. {% pending "the retention period for enquiries, including those that did not lead to any work." %}</p>

      <h2 id="security">How details are protected</h2>
      <p>We ask only for what an enquiry needs, never for passwords, OTPs or identity documents, and share details with a professional only with your agreement. The online form stays switched off until a secure destination is in place, and the safeguards for it will be described here. {% pending "the safeguards in place once a form backend exists." %}</p>

      <h2 id="site">Cookies and this website</h2>
      <p>As built today, this site sets no cookies of its own, loads no third-party fonts or scripts, and runs no analytics or advertising trackers. If that changes, this section must be updated first. Your hosting provider may keep ordinary server logs. Links to government portals, ICAI and social media take you to sites with their own policies.</p>

      <h2 id="age">Children</h2>
      <p>AccountOrbit is intended for adults enquiring for themselves or a business. Please do not submit details about a child.</p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We will update this page if our practices change, and show the date of the latest version here. {% pending "the effective date." %}</p>
